em related to the repository","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12082514052,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSbt78s8AAAAC0CyIhA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PerAlexandersson/RealRooted/labels/theory","name":"theory","color":"5319E7","default":false,"description":"Reusable mathematical framework, infrastructure, or general theorem","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":16,"created_at":"2026-10-09T13:35:57Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T12:39:48Z","closed_at":"2026-10-19T12:39:48Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PerAlexandersson/RealRooted/issues/1236","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"> **Refined target (2026-10-11).** Opposite termwise signs are not the obstruction: the exact simple-root condition is the combined compensation inequality `V(α) + W(α) h(α)/f′(α) < 0`. See the [division-free theorem route and consumer plan](https://github.com/PerAlexandersson/RealRooted/issues/1332#issuecomment-6108989056).\n\nSub-task of #1236, item 1.\n\n`P(n+2) = U P(n+1) + V P(n+1)' + W P n` with `V < 0` but `W > 0` at the roots. Rows: A046802, A056939, A111910, A123382, A318107, A318397, A271697. For A271697, `V = X − X²` vanishes at the root 0 of every row.\n\n**First step (research note):** at the roots of `P(n+1)`, compare the size of the two terms numerically for A046802, which is the type-B Eulerian-like family. Look for a published proof of each row (A046802 is classical) before designing a general step theorem.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PerAlexandersson/RealRooted/issues/1332/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0}